{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/nu58f2hs","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":675,"top":378,"width":525,"height":150},"name":"矩形 12","text":"0x10  UART data: read key / write byte\n0x11  UART status: rx_valid / tx_ready\n\nINP R0, 0x11   checks receive status\nOUP 0x10, R0   sends a state byte","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F5F8FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/wjy9sry9","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":62,"top":584,"width":1156,"height":58},"name":"矩形 13","text":"The board’s CP2103 bridges USB and UART. Verilog implements the UART controller and CPU port interface.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":20,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#A9BBCD","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/xk7qlczu","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":62,"top":643,"width":1156,"height":37},"name":"矩形 14","text":"The loader combines two 8-bit bytes into one 16-bit instruction and writes the 1K×16 program RAM.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F5F8FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/hwbqtkby","slideIndex":1,"text":"First explain SW7=1: the PC selects a program, and the loader combines two 8-bit bytes into each 16-bit instruction in the 1K×16 program RAM. With SW7=0, the CPU reads UART status at 0x11 and transfers data through 0x10. The PC draws the display; the CPU computes game rules. About 80 seconds.\n\nSources: runtime_soc.v; uart_port.v; io_decoder.v; program_loader.v."}
