{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/w72947yt","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":60,"top":534,"width":1160,"height":41},"name":"矩形 13","text":"All four logical lines use one routine; a tile merges at most once per move.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":21,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F5F8FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/x8vaxsfe","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":60,"top":590,"width":1160,"height":52},"name":"矩形 14","text":"Only a changed board triggers a new tile using random data from LFSR port 0x13.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":21,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#A9BBCD","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/a5kr2xg3","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":60,"top":645,"width":1160,"height":34},"name":"矩形 15","text":"The CPU computes the merged tile value by repeated doubling and updates the 16-bit score.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":19,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#F5F8FC","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/jyx0ra1s","slideIndex":3,"text":"Tiles are exponents: 0=empty, 1=2, 2=4. The direction changes the order in which four logical lines are read. The program skips zero cells, compares the current tile with the last output tile, and uses a merged flag to prevent a second merge. It writes back the board and spawns a tile only if the board changed. Repeated doubling computes the score increment. About 80 seconds.\n\nSources: game_2048.asm; lfsr8.v."}
